\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Baseline and component-ablation experiment under a shared SPBS incumbent. Pure SCIP and HEM-13D are the two baselines, RDMCT-HBS{} is the complete method, and the remaining entries are component-level ablations or single-component variants. Panels report mean PDI integrated using Eq.~\eqref  {eq:pdi-gap-en}, mean solution time, SCIP mean terminal relative gap from Eq.~\eqref  {eq:terminal-gap-en} (which may exceed 100\%), and proven-optimal rate over 2700 runs. Values and improvements over HEM are labeled directly. The blue diamond marks the complete RDMCT-HBS{}, orange and green circles mark the two baselines, and light-blue circles mark component ablations; line, marker, and hatch styles provide redundant encoding.}}{14}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:main-en-new}{{8}{14}{Baseline and component-ablation experiment under a shared SPBS incumbent. Pure SCIP and HEM-13D are the two baselines, \method {} is the complete method, and the remaining entries are component-level ablations or single-component variants. Panels report mean PDI integrated using Eq.~\eqref {eq:pdi-gap-en}, mean solution time, SCIP mean terminal relative gap from Eq.~\eqref {eq:terminal-gap-en} (which may exceed 100\%), and proven-optimal rate over 2700 runs. Values and improvements over HEM are labeled directly. The blue diamond marks the complete \method {}, orange and green circles mark the two baselines, and light-blue circles mark component ablations; line, marker, and hatch styles provide redundant encoding}{figure.8}{}}
